WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.210
Chadwick Boseman followed in the footsteps
of a whole host of elite superhero actors

00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:10.499
by getting seriously ripped for his role as
T'Challa in Black Panther—but his Hollywood

00:00:10.499 --> 00:00:14.940
fitness journey actually started well before
he joined the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:18.189
Here's some insight into how Chadwick got
chiseled.

00:00:18.189 --> 00:00:20.439
The path to Panther

00:00:20.439 --> 00:00:23.300
T'Challa isn't Boseman's first physically
demanding role.

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:27.539
In 2013, he portrayed Jackie Robinson in the
biographical drama 42.

00:00:27.539 --> 00:00:32.599
As well as capturing Robinson's off-field
contribution to the civil rights movement,

00:00:32.599 --> 00:00:36.300
Boseman needed to appear authentically athletic
for scenes on the field.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:40.579
To prepare, Boseman trained twice a day for
three and a half months, following the same

00:00:40.579 --> 00:00:42.300
techniques as the pros.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:47.269
In an interview with GQ, he referred to the
sessions as "madness" due to the strain such

00:00:47.269 --> 00:00:48.910
activity places on the body.

00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:53.469
Aside from swinging his hips and shuffling,
Boseman's appearance as the Godfather of Soul,

00:00:53.469 --> 00:00:57.920
James Brown, must have been a breeze compared
to 42, right?

00:00:57.920 --> 00:00:58.920
Wrong.

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:03.890
When portraying a musician as influential
as Brown, the pressure is on to not only sound

00:01:03.890 --> 00:01:05.770
the same, but to move the same, as well.

00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:11.770
Boseman had to do the splits while filming
Get On Up—not once, but 96 times.

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:15.990
The actor admitted that day's shooting was
harder than any activity he performed as Jackie

00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:17.700
Robinson.

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:18.740
Secret training

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:23.590
Unlike some of his fellow MCU stars, Boseman
has remained tight-lipped when it comes to

00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:25.890
divulging the secret of his regimen.

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:31.180
When asked by E! News prior to Civil War's
release, he refused to share any inside information

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:33.480
for those looking to emulate his results:

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:37.960
"A lot of strength and flexibility, but I'm
not going to say any more.

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:40.570
I can't say or reveal their training secrets."

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:45.530
Though Boseman hasn't disclosed the specifics
of his workout plan, all actors in the MCU

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:50.660
are notoriously put through their paces, and
he won't escape what Captain America himself,

00:01:50.660 --> 00:01:54.280
Chris Evans, refers to as "absolutely brutal"
sessions.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:55.340
"A couple of hours a day.

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:57.720
And it was, it was brutal.

00:01:57.720 --> 00:01:58.760
The tricky part was eating."

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:00.510
"Did you have to eat lots?"

00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:02.460
"Just eating everything all the time."

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:07.760
But the key to achieving Boseman's lean physique
likely lies more with classic bodybuilding

00:02:08.130 --> 00:02:13.180
techniques, including circuit training, and
a less substantial diet that still adds power

00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:14.620
to Black Panther's claws.

00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:19.549
While Evans needed to pack on the pounds in
a short span of time, Boseman's goal of remaining

00:02:19.549 --> 00:02:22.910
lean meant he could increase his body mass
at a slower rate.

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:27.769
This meant an extra emphasis on cardiovascular
and circuit training, to burn more calories.

00:02:27.769 --> 00:02:32.349
For explosive movements, Boseman would focus
on plyometric training, which increases power

00:02:32.349 --> 00:02:35.209
by working on "fast twitch" muscle fibers.

00:02:35.209 --> 00:02:39.879
Combat work likely tops it all off, with training
in a variety of martial arts.

00:02:39.879 --> 00:02:41.689
Losing muscle for Marshall

00:02:41.689 --> 00:02:47.520
Sandwiched between performances as Black Panther,
Boseman played Thurgood Marshall in the 2017

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:52.689
bio-pic Marshall, replacing Civil War's airport
battles with clashes in the courtroom.

00:02:52.689 --> 00:02:56.500
Understandably, Boseman would look out of
place as the future Supreme Court Justice

00:02:56.500 --> 00:03:01.110
if he maintained the mass, so to fit tailored
trousers and well-fitted blazers, the actor

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:04.950
needed to strip away 25 pounds of hard-earned
muscle.

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:09.530
Between the wrap on Marshall and the beginning
of Black Panther's production in January 2017,

00:03:09.530 --> 00:03:13.230
Boseman needed to recover lost muscle mass
to ensure his shoulders could carry the weight

00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:15.739
of expectation for his return as T'Challa.

00:03:15.739 --> 00:03:20.780
With the added spotlight and increased screen
time, Boseman's training regimen will presumably

00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:25.140
have been even more intense than his Civil
War workout, but the principles will remain

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:27.980
the same—a gradual progression of lean mass.

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:29.159
Thanks for watching!

